CHAPTER IV
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 7
(1) Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement prevention and mitigation efforts against the occurrence of violence towards women and children.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented in the form of:
a. Collecting data and information about women and children victims of violence;
b. Conducting education about anti-violence values towards women and children;
c. Conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
d. Training for PPT members;
e. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.
- 12 - (3) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence towards women and children, Regional Government is obligated to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving relevant community elements; b. encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims.

